1
00:00:01,001 --> 00:00:03,336
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:03,420 --> 00:00:06,464
[tense music playing]

3
00:00:20,353 --> 00:00:21,604
[screaming]

4
00:00:21,688 --> 00:00:23,773
[shattering sound]

5
00:00:27,360 --> 00:00:29,237
<i>Divine Oytengco and Miss Cora are dead.</i>

6
00:00:29,320 --> 00:00:30,947
<i>Now's the time. We have to arm ourselves.</i>

7
00:00:31,031 --> 00:00:32,449
<i>We have to fight back.</i>

8
00:00:32,532 --> 00:00:34,701
<i>Fine, go ahead and kill! Let's all kill!</i>

9
00:00:34,784 --> 00:00:36,286
<i>How will that make us</i>
<i>any different from them?!</i>

10
00:00:36,369 --> 00:00:38,079
<i>Later, you'll have a visitor.</i>

11
00:00:38,163 --> 00:00:39,497
<i>Who are you?!</i>

12
00:00:39,581 --> 00:00:41,082
<i>Why did you bring me here?!</i>

13
00:00:41,166 --> 00:00:42,417
<i>You won't be going to jail.</i>

14
00:00:42,500 --> 00:00:43,626
<i>Who helped me?</i>

15
00:00:43,710 --> 00:00:45,003
<i>What kind of nonsense is this?!</i>

16
00:00:45,086 --> 00:00:47,130
<i>How was Emilia's case whitewashed?!</i>

17
00:00:47,213 --> 00:00:48,298
<i>They got everything.</i>

18
00:00:48,381 --> 00:00:50,884
[Ivy] <i>Who else could've helped Emilia?!</i>

19
00:00:50,967 --> 00:00:53,261
[Julio] <i>Diego's group</i>

20
00:00:53,344 --> 00:00:55,430
<i>is planning to cause trouble again.</i>

21
00:00:55,513 --> 00:01:01,436
<i>And I choose you, Miss Aguas,</i>
<i>to carry out their punishment.</i>

22
00:01:01,519 --> 00:01:04,522
<i>Kill Diego's men.</i>

23
00:01:04,606 --> 00:01:06,316
<i>-No!</i>
<i>-Well, you choose.</i>

24
00:01:06,399 --> 00:01:09,027
<i>Either you kill them, or I'll kill you.</i>

25
00:01:09,110 --> 00:01:09,944
[Ivy] <i>Fine.</i>

26
00:01:10,028 --> 00:01:12,614
<i>If it'll make you happy, I'll do it.</i>

27
00:01:12,697 --> 00:01:14,157
[Jose] <i>You didn't help Emilia?</i>

28
00:01:14,240 --> 00:01:17,035
[Julio] <i>I just want to know who did.</i>

29
00:01:17,118 --> 00:01:20,997
<i>Because one day, that person</i>
<i>might be a threat to us.</i>

30
00:01:21,081 --> 00:01:22,916
[Camia] <i>Who were those men, Damian?</i>

31
00:01:22,999 --> 00:01:25,210
<i>The moment I find out</i>
<i>that you're lying to us,</i>

32
00:01:25,293 --> 00:01:27,295
<i>I will never forgive you.</i>

33
00:01:27,378 --> 00:01:29,631
[Ivy] <i>Diego! Julio's men abducted Anna</i>

34
00:01:29,714 --> 00:01:30,965
<i>and your supporters!</i>

35
00:01:31,049 --> 00:01:32,801
<i>-They're going to kill them!</i>
<i>-Help!</i>

36
00:01:32,884 --> 00:01:35,386
<i>-Help!</i>
<i>-Get us out!</i>

37
00:01:35,470 --> 00:01:36,638
<i>Ivy!</i>

38
00:01:36,721 --> 00:01:40,099
<i>Finally, I caught you red-handed.</i>

39
00:01:40,183 --> 00:01:41,059
<i>Traitor.</i>

40
00:01:41,142 --> 00:01:43,394
[suspenseful music playing]

41
00:01:44,354 --> 00:01:45,855
-Be careful, okay?
-[Diego panting]

42
00:01:45,939 --> 00:01:48,233
Protect Anna and my daughter.

43
00:01:48,316 --> 00:01:49,776
Yes, Auntie. Don't worry.

44
00:01:51,694 --> 00:01:52,612
Auntie…

45
00:01:52,695 --> 00:01:54,864
Diego Torillo! Stay where you are!

46
00:01:57,951 --> 00:01:59,786
[tense music playing]

47
00:02:02,664 --> 00:02:03,581
Hold on.

48
00:02:04,249 --> 00:02:05,458
What do you need?

49
00:02:05,542 --> 00:02:07,418
Shut up and come with us!

50
00:02:10,421 --> 00:02:11,548
Okay.

51
00:02:12,966 --> 00:02:15,593
Auntie, you take care of everything here.

52
00:02:18,763 --> 00:02:19,806
I'll go with you.

53
00:02:20,348 --> 00:02:23,309
[grunts, groans]

54
00:02:23,393 --> 00:02:24,894
-[Camia yelps]
-[grunts]

55
00:02:24,978 --> 00:02:26,146
-[groans]
-[Camia screams]

56
00:02:26,229 --> 00:02:30,275
-[grunts, groans]
-[suspenseful music playing]

57
00:02:33,278 --> 00:02:35,196
[Diego wheezing]

58
00:02:36,239 --> 00:02:37,157
Well?

59
00:02:37,240 --> 00:02:38,575
It's useless, Diego!

60
00:02:38,658 --> 00:02:40,827
[suspenseful music playing]

61
00:02:40,910 --> 00:02:42,912
[Diego panting]

62
00:02:43,955 --> 00:02:44,747
[panting]

63
00:02:50,628 --> 00:02:52,714
So, don't give me that look. Ivy, come on.

64
00:02:53,464 --> 00:02:55,341
Can you just drop the act?

65
00:02:55,425 --> 00:02:58,344
Stop lying to me because I know the truth!

66
00:02:59,012 --> 00:03:02,140
This conspiracy theory thing
was actually true!

67
00:03:03,016 --> 00:03:05,727
Nimfa was right when she said

68
00:03:05,810 --> 00:03:08,104
that you are Diego's spy.

69
00:03:08,938 --> 00:03:13,943
You are Camia and Lily Cruz's
ally, aren't you?

70
00:03:14,777 --> 00:03:17,405
And finally, I see the snake
for what she is!

71
00:03:17,488 --> 00:03:18,781
And worst of all,

72
00:03:18,865 --> 00:03:23,953
you damned woman ruined my son's life!

73
00:03:24,203 --> 00:03:25,622
You ruined my family!

74
00:03:25,705 --> 00:03:27,206
Why did you do this?!

75
00:03:27,290 --> 00:03:28,499
Why, Ivy? Why?!

76
00:03:29,125 --> 00:03:31,169
I don't know what you're talking about.

77
00:03:31,252 --> 00:03:33,046
-[gunshot]
-You liar!

78
00:03:34,088 --> 00:03:34,923
Well?!

79
00:03:35,006 --> 00:03:37,133
Are you still going to lie?

80
00:03:37,217 --> 00:03:38,927
[suspenseful music playing]

81
00:03:41,137 --> 00:03:43,973
[grunting, groaning]

82
00:03:52,982 --> 00:03:53,858
[grunts]

83
00:03:53,942 --> 00:03:55,068
[Emilia] You monster!

84
00:03:55,151 --> 00:03:57,153
[grunting]

85
00:03:57,904 --> 00:03:59,030
You!

86
00:04:01,115 --> 00:04:02,242
-[Emilia grunts]
-[Ivy yelps]

87
00:04:02,325 --> 00:04:03,952
-[Emilia grumbles]
-You monster!

88
00:04:06,913 --> 00:04:09,082
-You damned woman!
-[Ivy grunts]

89
00:04:09,374 --> 00:04:10,625
-Well?!
-Is that all you've got?!

90
00:04:10,708 --> 00:04:11,918
-Admit it!
-[groans]

91
00:04:12,001 --> 00:04:13,253
[panting]

92
00:04:13,336 --> 00:04:15,463
-Just admit it!
-No--

93
00:04:19,259 --> 00:04:20,093
Ouch!

94
00:04:20,176 --> 00:04:21,678
-You nutjob!
-[Emilia whines]

95
00:04:21,761 --> 00:04:26,015
-[grunts, groans]
-[suspenseful music playing]

96
00:04:34,649 --> 00:04:35,650
[grumbles]

97
00:04:35,733 --> 00:04:39,028
[suspenseful music playing]

98
00:04:47,745 --> 00:04:52,875
[grunting, groaning]

99
00:05:03,511 --> 00:05:07,890
-[labored breathing]
-[panting]

100
00:05:12,020 --> 00:05:13,813
-[grunts]
-[groans]

101
00:05:19,277 --> 00:05:20,486
-You traitor!
-[Ivy grunts]

102
00:05:20,570 --> 00:05:22,572
-Admit it!
-[Ivy groans]

103
00:05:22,655 --> 00:05:25,908
You are the traitor in this family!

104
00:05:27,160 --> 00:05:30,747
-[Emilia grumbles]
-[Ivy grunting]

105
00:05:31,831 --> 00:05:32,623
[Emilia grunts]

106
00:05:35,585 --> 00:05:37,670
-[Ivy panting]
-[Emilia groaning]

107
00:05:37,754 --> 00:05:39,630
-You want to hear the truth?
-[Emilia wheezing]

108
00:05:39,714 --> 00:05:40,631
-Answer!
-[groans]

109
00:05:40,715 --> 00:05:42,383
You want to hear it?!

110
00:05:42,467 --> 00:05:44,135
[gasps for air]

111
00:05:44,218 --> 00:05:46,929
Yes, Emilia. It's true!

112
00:05:47,013 --> 00:05:51,851
-[Emilia wheezing]
-I'm the traitor in your family!

113
00:05:51,934 --> 00:05:57,315
I, Ivy Aguas, am the traitor
in the Ardiente family!

114
00:05:57,398 --> 00:05:58,357
[Emilia whines]

115
00:05:58,441 --> 00:06:02,445
I'm allied with Diego, Lily,
and Camia Cruz.

116
00:06:02,528 --> 00:06:04,739
-You hear me, huh?
-[Emilia gasping for air]

117
00:06:04,822 --> 00:06:07,283
I'm the traitor in your family!

118
00:06:07,366 --> 00:06:10,745
-[Emilia grunts]
-I'm the traitor in your family!

119
00:06:12,622 --> 00:06:15,416
[dramatic music playing]

120
00:06:25,134 --> 00:06:28,930
[panting]

121
00:06:32,183 --> 00:06:34,227
[dramatic music playing]

122
00:06:35,728 --> 00:06:37,105
Stop resisting, Diego!

123
00:06:38,397 --> 00:06:39,398
Camia…

124
00:06:39,941 --> 00:06:41,901
I need to tell you the truth.

125
00:06:41,984 --> 00:06:43,986
[heavy sighing]

126
00:06:45,113 --> 00:06:47,323
I'm not as innocent as I've claimed.

127
00:06:48,241 --> 00:06:49,617
[inhales, exhales]

128
00:06:49,700 --> 00:06:50,785
I…

129
00:06:51,911 --> 00:06:53,913
I am the original Jaguar.

130
00:06:53,996 --> 00:06:56,958
[suspenseful music playing]

131
00:07:06,926 --> 00:07:08,136
[grunts]

132
00:07:08,219 --> 00:07:09,262
-Hey!
-Ah!

133
00:07:09,345 --> 00:07:12,723
-[screaming]
-[grunting]

134
00:07:14,851 --> 00:07:16,769
-[screaming]
-[groaning]

135
00:07:17,937 --> 00:07:20,314
[grunting, groaning]

136
00:07:20,398 --> 00:07:21,691
-Hey, you!
-[Camia yelps]

137
00:07:21,774 --> 00:07:23,067
[grunts]

138
00:07:24,610 --> 00:07:25,862
You! [screams]

139
00:07:25,945 --> 00:07:27,613
-[grunts]
-[groans]

140
00:07:27,697 --> 00:07:28,698
-Are you okay?!
-Yes.

141
00:07:28,781 --> 00:07:29,824
-Are you sure?
-Get down!

142
00:07:29,907 --> 00:07:30,825
[groans]

143
00:07:31,868 --> 00:07:33,369
[panting]

144
00:07:33,453 --> 00:07:35,079
Diego! Diego!

145
00:07:35,163 --> 00:07:36,622
Get inside. I can handle this.

146
00:07:36,706 --> 00:07:37,874
Auntie.

147
00:07:37,957 --> 00:07:39,041
Get inside!

148
00:07:41,294 --> 00:07:43,463
-[panting]
-[suspenseful music playing]

149
00:07:44,672 --> 00:07:45,590
[coughing]

150
00:07:49,010 --> 00:07:50,761
-Who's going first?!
-Get him!

151
00:07:50,845 --> 00:07:53,598
-Hey!
-[grunts, groans]

152
00:07:53,681 --> 00:07:54,640
[screams]

153
00:07:58,603 --> 00:08:00,354
-[screaming]
-[grunting]

154
00:08:06,486 --> 00:08:07,528
[grunts]

155
00:08:07,612 --> 00:08:08,863
[Camia gasps]

156
00:08:10,031 --> 00:08:11,616
Haven't had enough, huh?!

157
00:08:12,575 --> 00:08:13,326
Wait!

158
00:08:16,412 --> 00:08:17,622
[grunts, groans]

159
00:08:22,960 --> 00:08:26,047
[suspenseful music playing]

160
00:08:28,424 --> 00:08:30,551
[grunts, groans]

161
00:08:33,513 --> 00:08:34,889
-[grunts]
-Gimme that!

162
00:08:36,724 --> 00:08:37,683
Leave!

163
00:08:39,268 --> 00:08:40,311
I said, leave!

164
00:08:40,686 --> 00:08:41,938
Run! Let's go!

165
00:08:42,355 --> 00:08:43,814
-Come on!
-[grunting]

166
00:08:49,695 --> 00:08:51,739
[suspenseful music playing]

167
00:08:52,114 --> 00:08:53,157
[panting]

168
00:08:57,954 --> 00:09:00,122
-[Julio] Miss Aguas!
-[suspenseful music playing]

169
00:09:00,206 --> 00:09:01,040
Ha!

170
00:09:03,709 --> 00:09:05,503
You can't escape now.

171
00:09:05,920 --> 00:09:07,338
Just give up.

172
00:09:08,965 --> 00:09:13,427
We set the trap and
you jumped right into it.

173
00:09:14,178 --> 00:09:17,682
We told you to kill Diego's people.

174
00:09:18,266 --> 00:09:19,517
But in the process,

175
00:09:19,600 --> 00:09:23,062
Emilia followed you, because we knew that…

176
00:09:24,522 --> 00:09:27,066
you'd rescue those people,

177
00:09:27,149 --> 00:09:29,235
and you wouldn't let them die because…

178
00:09:31,112 --> 00:09:32,822
you really are a traitor.

179
00:09:33,864 --> 00:09:36,534
And we were right all along.

180
00:09:37,159 --> 00:09:38,494
Now…

181
00:09:38,578 --> 00:09:43,082
No snake will leave this place alive.

182
00:09:45,459 --> 00:09:46,419
[sighs]

183
00:09:47,545 --> 00:09:48,546
Colonel.

184
00:09:52,675 --> 00:09:54,427
[suspenseful music playing]

185
00:09:55,469 --> 00:09:56,554
[grunting]

186
00:10:01,726 --> 00:10:03,603
-[Julio grunts]
-[loud thud]

187
00:10:08,482 --> 00:10:09,442
Take her!

188
00:10:10,443 --> 00:10:12,486
[panting]

189
00:10:15,072 --> 00:10:16,699
Are you okay, Damian?

190
00:10:17,116 --> 00:10:18,200
Are you injured?

191
00:10:20,870 --> 00:10:21,954
Mr. Dante?

192
00:10:23,581 --> 00:10:24,582
Diego, no.

193
00:10:25,291 --> 00:10:26,542
He's Damian.

194
00:10:26,626 --> 00:10:28,085
He's Lily's uncle.

195
00:10:28,753 --> 00:10:30,254
Dante is his twin brother.

196
00:10:30,338 --> 00:10:33,799
It's a long story,
but he knows that Ivy is Lily.

197
00:10:34,383 --> 00:10:37,261
[dramatic music playing]

198
00:10:38,679 --> 00:10:40,056
Auntie, I need to go.

199
00:10:40,139 --> 00:10:42,391
Mr. Damian, please take care
of Aunt Camia.

200
00:10:42,975 --> 00:10:44,268
-Diego, be careful.
-I will.

201
00:10:44,352 --> 00:10:45,895
[panting]

202
00:10:46,771 --> 00:10:48,272
[motorcycle engine starts]

203
00:10:49,815 --> 00:10:52,485
[motorcycle engine revving]

204
00:10:59,533 --> 00:11:00,368
Come on.

205
00:11:00,993 --> 00:11:02,244
Let's get inside.

206
00:11:03,537 --> 00:11:04,455
Come on.

207
00:11:04,538 --> 00:11:05,790
I need water.

208
00:11:09,627 --> 00:11:10,586
[Emilia] Papa!

209
00:11:11,253 --> 00:11:12,380
Papa, wait!

210
00:11:13,422 --> 00:11:15,383
Emilia, you're here?

211
00:11:15,466 --> 00:11:17,885
Yes. I am here, Papa!

212
00:11:19,387 --> 00:11:22,890
And I'm the reason why that snake is here,

213
00:11:22,973 --> 00:11:25,351
and we caught her red-handed!

214
00:11:25,434 --> 00:11:28,062
It's because of me, Papa! Me!

215
00:11:28,813 --> 00:11:34,110
Emilia, no one is taking
the credit away from you.

216
00:11:35,277 --> 00:11:36,320
To tell you the truth…

217
00:11:37,405 --> 00:11:39,240
I'm very proud of you!

218
00:11:39,907 --> 00:11:40,866
Good job!

219
00:11:41,242 --> 00:11:42,118
Good job.

220
00:11:42,201 --> 00:11:43,828
Papa, I don't need your praise.

221
00:11:43,911 --> 00:11:46,497
I need to know where
you're bringing that woman!

222
00:11:46,580 --> 00:11:47,748
[Julio] Wait, wait.

223
00:11:50,501 --> 00:11:51,627
This woman…

224
00:11:52,336 --> 00:11:56,132
does not deserve any special treatment.

225
00:11:56,966 --> 00:11:59,510
There will be no ceremonies.

226
00:11:59,593 --> 00:12:01,470
There will be no rituals.

227
00:12:02,346 --> 00:12:04,390
She will die with a bullet

228
00:12:04,473 --> 00:12:06,684
to the back of her head,

229
00:12:06,767 --> 00:12:09,562
just like any other traitor.

230
00:12:09,645 --> 00:12:12,273
No, Papa! I want to kill her!

231
00:12:12,356 --> 00:12:13,983
-I'll kill her!
-No!

232
00:12:14,275 --> 00:12:16,277
Can you just stop it?!

233
00:12:16,360 --> 00:12:18,446
Take it easy, Emilia.

234
00:12:18,529 --> 00:12:20,281
You know what? That's your problem.

235
00:12:20,906 --> 00:12:25,077
You get so high-strung
that you end up screwing things up.

236
00:12:26,954 --> 00:12:29,081
You can't just kill her here.

237
00:12:29,165 --> 00:12:32,334
It'll leave a lot of evidence against us.

238
00:12:33,335 --> 00:12:36,505
Let the professionals take care of this.

239
00:12:36,589 --> 00:12:39,425
No, Papa. I will kill her!

240
00:12:39,508 --> 00:12:41,886
I will kill that woman
because she's the reason

241
00:12:41,969 --> 00:12:45,389
why Arnaldo went crazy
and why I went to jail!

242
00:12:45,473 --> 00:12:47,308
-I will kill you!
-Please, please!

243
00:12:47,975 --> 00:12:49,351
I am the head of this family.

244
00:12:49,435 --> 00:12:52,521
I will decide how she is going to die.

245
00:12:52,605 --> 00:12:54,815
You may be the head of this family, Papa,

246
00:12:54,899 --> 00:12:59,361
but you're also the reason
why that woman betrayed us!

247
00:12:59,445 --> 00:13:02,490
Because you allowed her
to be close to you!

248
00:13:02,573 --> 00:13:04,909
You sound like a broken record,
repeating yourself.

249
00:13:04,992 --> 00:13:05,993
[Ivy chuckles]

250
00:13:06,076 --> 00:13:07,536
And what is so funny, huh?

251
00:13:08,746 --> 00:13:10,289
What's so funny?!

252
00:13:10,372 --> 00:13:11,874
Look at you two.

253
00:13:11,957 --> 00:13:15,544
You're like two children
fighting over candy.

254
00:13:15,628 --> 00:13:18,506
How about you guys just fight over

255
00:13:18,589 --> 00:13:23,093
who I'm going to kill first
once I get out of this?

256
00:13:23,177 --> 00:13:25,888
-You're getting on my nerves!
-Stop it! Stop it!

257
00:13:25,971 --> 00:13:27,223
-Enough!
-[Emilia groans]

258
00:13:27,306 --> 00:13:28,182
Enough!

259
00:13:28,265 --> 00:13:30,976
You really make my blood boil!

260
00:13:31,060 --> 00:13:32,895
Is that all you can do, Emilia?!

261
00:13:32,978 --> 00:13:34,396
-Enough!
-Come on, Papa!

262
00:13:34,480 --> 00:13:36,690
Don't take this away from me!

263
00:13:36,774 --> 00:13:38,817
We always do what you want!

264
00:13:38,901 --> 00:13:42,863
Now you won't even let me kill her, Papa?!

265
00:13:42,947 --> 00:13:44,907
Come on! I am your daughter!

266
00:13:44,990 --> 00:13:46,951
Give me this chance, Papa!

267
00:13:47,034 --> 00:13:52,373
Put your entitlement issues on the side!

268
00:13:53,874 --> 00:13:55,709
You're such a spoiled brat!

269
00:13:59,505 --> 00:14:01,006
And you, Miss Aguas.

270
00:14:01,882 --> 00:14:03,050
Yes, Governor?

271
00:14:03,968 --> 00:14:06,136
You are mine!

272
00:14:06,220 --> 00:14:07,429
Sure, take me!

273
00:14:07,513 --> 00:14:09,306
I'm all yours.

274
00:14:10,558 --> 00:14:12,685
Sanggano, make sure she doesn't escape.

275
00:14:12,768 --> 00:14:15,854
And take her car with you.

276
00:14:15,938 --> 00:14:18,023
I don't want to leave any evidence.

277
00:14:18,107 --> 00:14:20,359
-Aww, poor Emilia.
-Yes, boss.

278
00:14:20,442 --> 00:14:21,777
Deprived of one more thing.

279
00:14:21,861 --> 00:14:23,070
Well, what's new?

280
00:14:23,153 --> 00:14:24,655
-As always.
-[Emilia groans]

281
00:14:24,738 --> 00:14:25,698
[Ivy grunts]

282
00:14:25,781 --> 00:14:28,117
I will see you in hell!

283
00:14:28,200 --> 00:14:29,285
Can't wait!

284
00:14:29,368 --> 00:14:31,871
I'll roll out the red carpet for you!

285
00:14:31,954 --> 00:14:33,289
Yeah, you should!

286
00:14:33,372 --> 00:14:34,373
Get in!

287
00:14:36,458 --> 00:14:37,334
[Ivy grunts]

288
00:14:41,881 --> 00:14:46,051
[suspenseful music playing]

289
00:14:48,596 --> 00:14:50,639
-Damian, give me your hand.
-[Damian groaning]

290
00:14:51,181 --> 00:14:52,016
It hurts.

291
00:14:52,892 --> 00:14:54,643
Oh, ouch, ouch. Be gentle.

292
00:14:54,727 --> 00:14:55,769
-There?
-It hurts.

293
00:14:57,062 --> 00:14:57,980
Damian?

294
00:14:59,523 --> 00:15:01,859
Thank you very much for saving me.

295
00:15:04,069 --> 00:15:09,283
And forgive me for thinking badly of you.

296
00:15:10,951 --> 00:15:13,579
Don't worry about it. I can't blame you

297
00:15:13,662 --> 00:15:16,916
because you know
the stuff I've done before.

298
00:15:16,999 --> 00:15:18,042
And…

299
00:15:18,375 --> 00:15:20,920
I can't say my face
doesn't look suspicious.

300
00:15:23,756 --> 00:15:24,715
Damian…

301
00:15:25,841 --> 00:15:27,509
I wish Dante were still alive…

302
00:15:28,260 --> 00:15:30,846
so he could see how much you've changed.

303
00:15:31,263 --> 00:15:33,223
He always dreamt of seeing you change.

304
00:15:33,933 --> 00:15:36,852
[soft music playing]

305
00:15:38,479 --> 00:15:41,357
[Damian] <i>Now, how am I supposed</i>
<i>to tell you the truth</i>

306
00:15:41,440 --> 00:15:43,192
<i>that I'm a criminal?</i>

307
00:15:43,275 --> 00:15:45,110
<i>That I'm a murderer.</i>

308
00:15:45,903 --> 00:15:47,488
<i>That I am Jaguar.</i>

309
00:15:50,449 --> 00:15:51,575
Where else does it hurt?

310
00:15:52,076 --> 00:15:53,410
I got elbowed here.

311
00:15:53,494 --> 00:15:54,620
You were elbowed?

312
00:15:55,496 --> 00:15:56,580
-It hurts.
-All right.

313
00:15:56,664 --> 00:15:58,040
-Ouch…
-There.

314
00:15:59,625 --> 00:16:03,587
And then, after that, I got hit here.

315
00:16:03,671 --> 00:16:05,005
You were hit there?

316
00:16:05,673 --> 00:16:06,966
Let's put some ice on it.

317
00:16:08,175 --> 00:16:09,426
-Here.
-Ouch. Be gentle.

318
00:16:10,135 --> 00:16:11,261
Hold it.

319
00:16:11,345 --> 00:16:12,680
-Huh?
-Take it.

320
00:16:13,305 --> 00:16:14,848
Let me clean you up.

321
00:16:16,725 --> 00:16:19,478
[soft music playing]

322
00:16:33,033 --> 00:16:35,202
[Loring panting]

323
00:16:35,285 --> 00:16:36,161
Camia!

324
00:16:36,620 --> 00:16:37,621
Oh, Camia!

325
00:16:37,705 --> 00:16:40,708
I thought we wouldn't get out--[gasps]

326
00:16:40,791 --> 00:16:43,210
Oh, thank goodness you're all safe.

327
00:16:43,293 --> 00:16:44,128
Uh…

328
00:16:45,004 --> 00:16:45,796
Oh!

329
00:16:45,879 --> 00:16:48,215
-Miss Loring, Mr. Pandoy…
-Loring?

330
00:16:48,298 --> 00:16:49,049
Anna…

331
00:16:49,675 --> 00:16:51,844
This is Damian, Dante's brother.

332
00:16:52,261 --> 00:16:53,512
Good evening.

333
00:16:53,804 --> 00:16:55,597
[breath quivering]

334
00:16:55,681 --> 00:16:56,932
[Pandoy] Loring?

335
00:16:57,683 --> 00:17:00,019
I thought he was Lily's father.

336
00:17:00,102 --> 00:17:01,020
[Pandoy] Huh?

337
00:17:01,937 --> 00:17:03,105
He looks just like him.

338
00:17:03,897 --> 00:17:07,943
Wait, let's all go inside
so we can clean your wounds.

339
00:17:08,569 --> 00:17:10,904
[pensive music playing]

340
00:17:27,171 --> 00:17:29,339
[motorcycle engine revving]

341
00:17:33,761 --> 00:17:34,720
What happened here?

342
00:17:34,803 --> 00:17:37,556
We don't know.
We just saw the house burning.

343
00:17:41,268 --> 00:17:43,270
Does anyone know what happened here?

344
00:17:43,353 --> 00:17:44,146
No, Diego.

345
00:17:44,229 --> 00:17:46,440
We don't really come here often.

346
00:17:46,815 --> 00:17:48,150
Whose house is this?

347
00:17:48,233 --> 00:17:50,527
We don't know. This is an abandoned house.

348
00:17:50,611 --> 00:17:52,279
No one's lived here for years.

349
00:17:54,406 --> 00:17:56,700
[ominous music playing]

350
00:18:02,831 --> 00:18:04,833
[voice prompt] <i>The subscriber</i>
<i>cannot be reached.</i>

351
00:18:04,917 --> 00:18:06,585
<i>Please try again later.</i>

352
00:18:18,722 --> 00:18:24,812
-[chains rattling]
-[metal wheels clunking]

353
00:18:25,604 --> 00:18:32,152
[Ivy's breath quivering]

354
00:18:44,248 --> 00:18:46,500
Well, hello, Miss Aguas!

355
00:18:46,875 --> 00:18:48,627
[breath quivering]

356
00:18:48,710 --> 00:18:50,462
Uh… Let's clear things up.

357
00:18:50,546 --> 00:18:52,297
Now that you've been caught…

358
00:18:52,381 --> 00:18:55,759
and are about to die…

359
00:18:59,304 --> 00:19:03,142
Maybe you'll have nothing left
to lose if you tell me…

360
00:19:04,726 --> 00:19:07,646
why you loathe my family so much.

361
00:19:07,729 --> 00:19:09,022
I mean…

362
00:19:09,773 --> 00:19:12,317
What is it that keeps

363
00:19:12,401 --> 00:19:17,364
the fire burning inside you, Miss Aguas?

364
00:19:18,699 --> 00:19:23,162
Did I, or did we, mistreat you
when you were younger?

365
00:19:23,245 --> 00:19:25,372
[suspenseful music playing]

366
00:19:25,789 --> 00:19:26,915
Or did I…

367
00:19:28,292 --> 00:19:33,172
Did I hurt your relatives?

368
00:19:36,800 --> 00:19:38,177
Your parents, perhaps?

369
00:19:40,596 --> 00:19:44,349
Uh… What's your story? Please let me know.

370
00:19:45,350 --> 00:19:47,019
I… [breath quivers]

371
00:19:47,102 --> 00:19:51,565
I have nothing personal
against you, Governor.

372
00:19:52,232 --> 00:19:53,692
[Ivy breathes heavily]

373
00:19:53,775 --> 00:19:58,322
I just want your money and your power.

374
00:19:58,947 --> 00:20:02,326
Nothing more, nothing less.

375
00:20:03,160 --> 00:20:04,286
Weird!

376
00:20:05,454 --> 00:20:09,958
Out of all the powerful
people in the world…

377
00:20:11,043 --> 00:20:12,711
why did you choose my family?

378
00:20:13,045 --> 00:20:15,714
Because you have a psychotic daughter.

379
00:20:16,798 --> 00:20:20,010
And a crazy, obsessive grandson!

380
00:20:20,969 --> 00:20:22,387
I thought it'd be easy.

381
00:20:23,889 --> 00:20:26,600
But I was wrong.

382
00:20:28,018 --> 00:20:30,062
Well, my bad!

383
00:20:31,480 --> 00:20:34,483
Thank you for saying
you underestimated me.

384
00:20:34,566 --> 00:20:36,401
-[Ivy trembling]
-Uh… but…

385
00:20:37,110 --> 00:20:38,946
why do I get the feeling that

386
00:20:39,029 --> 00:20:41,198
everything that comes out of your mouth

387
00:20:42,282 --> 00:20:44,034
is nothing but lies?

388
00:20:44,660 --> 00:20:45,494
Huh?

389
00:20:47,162 --> 00:20:48,080
Well…

390
00:20:48,914 --> 00:20:51,208
It doesn't really matter to me, you know?

391
00:20:51,291 --> 00:20:54,962
Whatever the truth is,
it doesn't really affect me.

392
00:20:55,045 --> 00:20:58,674
Because, after all, you're about to die.

393
00:20:59,383 --> 00:21:04,721
You can bring your secrets to your grave.

394
00:21:05,806 --> 00:21:07,057
But I'm telling you,

395
00:21:07,140 --> 00:21:11,228
I'll be able to sleep soundly…

396
00:21:11,937 --> 00:21:17,818
knowing that you are dead!

397
00:21:19,361 --> 00:21:21,571
[tense music playing]

398
00:21:23,156 --> 00:21:26,576
Enjoy your final hours on Earth,
Miss Aguas!

399
00:21:28,412 --> 00:21:31,748
It was fun going up against you.

400
00:21:31,832 --> 00:21:33,208
And, I must admit…

401
00:21:33,750 --> 00:21:37,963
you were a very worthy opponent.

402
00:21:41,717 --> 00:21:45,679
Goodbye, Your Lying Majesty!

403
00:21:47,514 --> 00:21:49,224
Look who's talking!

404
00:21:50,809 --> 00:21:53,729
Don't celebrate just yet, old man Julio!

405
00:21:56,440 --> 00:22:01,278
Because I'm not through with you!

406
00:22:02,029 --> 00:22:05,282
Where does she get her energy?

407
00:22:05,949 --> 00:22:07,659
[menacing laugh]

408
00:22:08,452 --> 00:22:12,956
-[Ivy's breath quivering]
-[Julio laughs menacingly]

409
00:22:14,041 --> 00:22:18,170
[suspenseful music playing]

410
00:22:19,171 --> 00:22:21,006
Ivy was no longer there when I arrived.

411
00:22:21,089 --> 00:22:23,050
And I can't reach her cell phone number.

412
00:22:24,051 --> 00:22:28,055
We couldn't reach her landline
and safehouse numbers, either.

413
00:22:28,472 --> 00:22:30,640
Maybe she's back at the Ardientes' place.

414
00:22:31,141 --> 00:22:32,559
Before we parted ways,

415
00:22:32,642 --> 00:22:35,562
she told me that she'd return
to the Ardientes

416
00:22:35,645 --> 00:22:36,980
so she wouldn't get caught.

417
00:22:37,064 --> 00:22:40,275
But why hasn't she called yet? [huffs]

418
00:22:40,358 --> 00:22:43,236
Auntie, maybe she hasn't
found the chance yet.

419
00:22:44,071 --> 00:22:47,783
I won't be at ease until
I'm sure my daughter's safe!

420
00:22:47,866 --> 00:22:51,369
Auntie Camia, Lily has risked
blowing her cover so many times.

421
00:22:51,453 --> 00:22:53,246
But she always managed
to get out of danger.

422
00:22:53,330 --> 00:22:55,916
If we don't trust Lily,

423
00:22:55,999 --> 00:22:58,418
we might just put her in trouble.

424
00:22:59,753 --> 00:23:01,213
[Loring] Anna is right.

425
00:23:01,296 --> 00:23:04,049
We shouldn't look for Ivy at this point,

426
00:23:04,132 --> 00:23:05,759
or her cover might get blown.

427
00:23:06,134 --> 00:23:09,221
The only thing we can do now is wait.

428
00:23:11,223 --> 00:23:13,892
Waiting isn't an option for me
when it comes to my daughter.

429
00:23:16,978 --> 00:23:18,146
Auntie, don't worry.

430
00:23:18,396 --> 00:23:20,941
I'll come up with another plan
to find her.

431
00:23:24,236 --> 00:23:26,947
[slow tense music playing]

432
00:23:34,121 --> 00:23:36,206
I hate you, Papa. I hate you!

433
00:23:36,289 --> 00:23:38,667
You're so selfish!

434
00:23:38,750 --> 00:23:42,003
You deprived me of everything,

435
00:23:42,087 --> 00:23:44,965
including my real mother!

436
00:23:45,048 --> 00:23:50,011
You always take everything away from me!

437
00:23:50,095 --> 00:23:51,805
Even the chance to kill Ivy Aguas!

438
00:23:51,888 --> 00:23:54,099
It always has to be you!

439
00:23:55,058 --> 00:23:56,393
[inhales sharply]

440
00:23:56,476 --> 00:23:58,103
But this time around,

441
00:23:58,186 --> 00:24:00,355
I won't let things go your way.

442
00:24:00,438 --> 00:24:03,608
I'm not gonna let you do it
because I am going to do it!

443
00:24:03,692 --> 00:24:05,986
I am going to kill Ivy…

444
00:24:06,862 --> 00:24:08,029
…Aguas!

445
00:24:08,113 --> 00:24:11,658
[heavy breathing]

446
00:24:11,741 --> 00:24:12,909
[phone ringing]

447
00:24:13,577 --> 00:24:14,411
Hello?

448
00:24:14,494 --> 00:24:15,412
Hello, officer.

449
00:24:15,495 --> 00:24:17,247
I would like to report a missing person.

450
00:24:17,330 --> 00:24:18,582
What's their name?

451
00:24:18,665 --> 00:24:19,708
Ivy Aguas.

452
00:24:20,083 --> 00:24:22,460
She went missing on her way
to the Ardientes' place.

453
00:24:22,544 --> 00:24:25,755
We suspect there's foul play involved.

454
00:24:25,839 --> 00:24:27,007
May I know your name?

455
00:24:28,216 --> 00:24:29,467
Just a concerned citizen.

456
00:24:29,551 --> 00:24:33,346
<i>Please go to the Ardientes</i>
<i>and look for Ivy Aguas.</i>

457
00:24:33,430 --> 00:24:34,556
Thank you.

458
00:24:35,765 --> 00:24:41,771
[tense music playing]

459
00:24:43,523 --> 00:24:45,609
How can I help you, gentlemen?

460
00:24:46,359 --> 00:24:48,445
Sorry to bother you, Governor,

461
00:24:48,528 --> 00:24:51,323
but we received a report saying

462
00:24:51,406 --> 00:24:53,617
Miss Ivy Aguas is missing.

463
00:24:53,700 --> 00:24:54,910
[scoffs]

464
00:24:56,119 --> 00:24:57,037
Why?

465
00:24:57,120 --> 00:25:00,540
Does my place look like
a lost-and-found office to you?

466
00:25:01,458 --> 00:25:05,128
I don't know where Miss Aguas is.

467
00:25:06,338 --> 00:25:11,301
I'm no longer associated with her,
so she's not my responsibility.

468
00:25:12,219 --> 00:25:17,390
Perhaps it would be better
for you to look elsewhere.

469
00:25:17,474 --> 00:25:19,893
We're sorry, Governor.
Thank you for your time.

470
00:25:19,976 --> 00:25:21,102
All right.

471
00:25:21,603 --> 00:25:22,854
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

472
00:25:28,109 --> 00:25:32,155
I'm sure Diego and his group
are the ones looking for Ivy.

473
00:25:33,740 --> 00:25:37,410
Make sure they don't find her.

474
00:25:37,953 --> 00:25:40,038
Because if that woman breaks free,

475
00:25:40,121 --> 00:25:42,666
I'll make you take her place in her grave.

476
00:25:43,667 --> 00:25:44,793
Yes, Governor.

477
00:25:49,714 --> 00:25:50,966
[Diego] <i>Yes.</i>

478
00:25:52,509 --> 00:25:54,344
Ivy Aguas is on our side.

479
00:25:54,427 --> 00:25:56,012
[indistinct chatter]

480
00:25:56,096 --> 00:25:58,139
She is pretending to help the Ardientes

481
00:25:58,223 --> 00:26:00,058
so she can infiltrate their world.

482
00:26:00,141 --> 00:26:04,437
She is the heart, mind,
and soul of our cause.

483
00:26:05,397 --> 00:26:06,564
And right now…

484
00:26:07,232 --> 00:26:09,317
she could be in danger.

485
00:26:11,569 --> 00:26:13,280
That's why she needs our help.

486
00:26:13,363 --> 00:26:16,116
She needs help from each
and every one of us.

487
00:26:16,199 --> 00:26:17,659
We must find her.

488
00:26:18,702 --> 00:26:22,414
One of us has to stake out
the Ardientes' residence

489
00:26:22,497 --> 00:26:25,000
so we can find out if she's there.

490
00:26:26,501 --> 00:26:27,711
I'll do it, Diego.

491
00:26:28,420 --> 00:26:29,963
-But, son…
-I can do this, Mom.

492
00:26:30,672 --> 00:26:32,215
The Ardientes don't know me.

493
00:26:32,299 --> 00:26:34,092
So, I can move freely
outside their mansion.

494
00:26:34,175 --> 00:26:36,094
A-Are you sure?

495
00:26:36,177 --> 00:26:37,804
It's going to be dangerous.

496
00:26:37,887 --> 00:26:40,056
Miss Aguas risked her life for us.

497
00:26:40,140 --> 00:26:43,018
So, it's only right we return the favor.

498
00:26:43,101 --> 00:26:45,103
I'll help you find her.

499
00:26:45,186 --> 00:26:46,354
Diego.

500
00:26:47,439 --> 00:26:49,649
Leave the search for Ivy to us.

501
00:26:50,233 --> 00:26:54,738
You should focus on stopping
Julio once and for all.

502
00:26:54,821 --> 00:26:55,822
-Yeah.
-That's right.

503
00:26:55,905 --> 00:26:58,074
-That's right.
-I agree!

504
00:26:58,450 --> 00:27:00,410
[tense music playing]

505
00:27:07,751 --> 00:27:10,837
[pensive music playing]

506
00:27:16,593 --> 00:27:17,635
Nanny.

507
00:27:21,139 --> 00:27:23,058
Nanny, is there something wrong?

508
00:27:23,141 --> 00:27:24,184
Hmm?

509
00:27:24,893 --> 00:27:26,770
I noticed you keep looking
at Mister Damian.

510
00:27:27,395 --> 00:27:28,229
Huh?

511
00:27:28,563 --> 00:27:30,148
Well, you see…

512
00:27:30,231 --> 00:27:33,693
he looks exactly like Lily's father.

513
00:27:34,235 --> 00:27:37,155
It makes me recall how Mister Dante

514
00:27:37,238 --> 00:27:39,282
was a very kind man.

515
00:27:39,949 --> 00:27:41,743
He was very brave too.

516
00:27:41,826 --> 00:27:44,704
And that was the reason
the Ardientes had him killed.

517
00:27:45,413 --> 00:27:48,333
I just hope he's as kind as Mister Dante.

518
00:27:49,042 --> 00:27:52,253
I'm sure Lily will be hurt
if he betrays us.

519
00:27:52,337 --> 00:27:55,215
There are so many
deceitful people in the world.

520
00:27:55,298 --> 00:27:57,550
I hope he's not one of them too.

521
00:27:59,677 --> 00:28:02,180
Speaking of deceitful, Mr. Pandoy…

522
00:28:03,223 --> 00:28:06,142
What's our next move against Julio?

523
00:28:06,226 --> 00:28:07,477
I have a plan.

524
00:28:09,562 --> 00:28:11,356
[suspenseful music playing]

525
00:28:21,699 --> 00:28:23,076
Attorney.

526
00:28:23,159 --> 00:28:24,160
Diego.

527
00:28:24,577 --> 00:28:26,955
Vice Governor Ruiz
is already waiting downstairs.

528
00:28:27,038 --> 00:28:28,581
We must convince him

529
00:28:28,665 --> 00:28:31,376
to form an alliance
with us against Julio Ardiente.

530
00:28:31,459 --> 00:28:33,753
Well, Vice Governor Ruiz
does have a reputation

531
00:28:33,837 --> 00:28:36,965
for being intolerant of
corrupt government practices.

532
00:28:37,048 --> 00:28:38,758
You're very much alike, Diego.

533
00:28:38,842 --> 00:28:41,845
Which is why I'm very
confident he'll listen to you.

534
00:28:41,928 --> 00:28:43,471
We can trust him.

535
00:28:44,305 --> 00:28:45,265
I hope so.

536
00:28:48,893 --> 00:28:49,811
Mr. Diego Torillo…

537
00:28:49,894 --> 00:28:52,063
-…and Attorney Fisher.
-Yes?

538
00:28:52,147 --> 00:28:54,107
Vice Governor Ruiz is waiting for you.

539
00:28:54,190 --> 00:28:55,066
Follow me.

540
00:28:57,235 --> 00:28:58,278
[gunshot]

541
00:29:03,700 --> 00:29:05,285
[gunshots]

542
00:29:06,870 --> 00:29:08,413
The Vice Governor's guests.

543
00:29:08,830 --> 00:29:10,415
[knocking on door]

544
00:29:10,999 --> 00:29:13,209
[suspenseful music playing]

545
00:29:14,836 --> 00:29:16,588
[gunshots]

546
00:29:19,466 --> 00:29:22,093
[gunshots]

547
00:29:23,011 --> 00:29:24,679
You haven't lost your touch,
Vice Governor.

548
00:29:24,763 --> 00:29:26,848
[suspenseful music playing]

549
00:29:30,185 --> 00:29:31,811
Vice Governor, they're here.

550
00:29:38,818 --> 00:29:41,529
[suspenseful music playing]

551
00:29:50,789 --> 00:29:51,706
Nurse?

552
00:29:52,874 --> 00:29:55,335
Get Arnaldo dressed. We're going out.

553
00:29:55,418 --> 00:29:56,711
Yes, Governor.

554
00:29:58,546 --> 00:30:00,548
Arnaldo, my grandson…

555
00:30:01,466 --> 00:30:03,218
I have a surprise for you.

556
00:30:04,761 --> 00:30:06,346
We're going to meet…

557
00:30:07,138 --> 00:30:08,681
the woman who hurt you.

558
00:30:08,765 --> 00:30:12,519
-[heart monitor beeping]
-Miss Aguas.

559
00:30:13,102 --> 00:30:14,354
Do you remember her?

560
00:30:15,522 --> 00:30:18,817
I want you to witness her death…

561
00:30:20,193 --> 00:30:23,905
…as revenge for what she did to you.

562
00:30:24,823 --> 00:30:26,950
[foreboding music playing]

563
00:30:42,966 --> 00:30:44,342
[goon] You have to eat, Miss Aguas.

564
00:30:44,759 --> 00:30:45,844
Governor's orders.

565
00:30:46,135 --> 00:30:47,554
Don't try to fight back.

566
00:30:47,637 --> 00:30:49,472
[tense music playing]

567
00:30:49,973 --> 00:30:52,141
[heavy breathing]

568
00:30:53,852 --> 00:30:54,853
Tie her up.

569
00:30:55,311 --> 00:30:56,396
Nice and tight.

570
00:30:56,479 --> 00:30:57,939
Miss Aguas.

571
00:30:58,481 --> 00:30:59,524
Eat up.

572
00:31:02,110 --> 00:31:03,862
-[utensils clanking]
-[groans]

573
00:31:03,945 --> 00:31:08,408
-[suspenseful music playing]
-[grunting, groaning]

574
00:31:15,665 --> 00:31:17,250
-Where's the rope?
-Tie her up!

575
00:31:17,750 --> 00:31:21,588
[suspenseful music playing]

576
00:31:22,589 --> 00:31:23,840
Hey, hurry up.

577
00:31:25,174 --> 00:31:26,718
How many boxes are still there?

578
00:31:27,760 --> 00:31:28,803
Get them.

579
00:31:35,894 --> 00:31:37,061
[line ringing]

580
00:31:37,145 --> 00:31:37,896
Hello?

581
00:31:37,979 --> 00:31:39,939
<i>Miss Camia, I've been here a while now.</i>

582
00:31:40,023 --> 00:31:41,733
But I haven't seen Miss Aguas.

583
00:31:42,358 --> 00:31:43,818
What's going on there?

584
00:31:45,194 --> 00:31:46,988
<i>I think the Ardientes are busy</i>

585
00:31:47,071 --> 00:31:49,490
<i>preparing for the province's</i>
<i>centennial celebration.</i>

586
00:31:49,824 --> 00:31:52,368
Okay, come back now before they catch you.

587
00:31:52,952 --> 00:31:54,203
What about Miss Aguas?

588
00:31:54,662 --> 00:31:57,498
[sighs] I don't think
she's at their mansion.

589
00:31:58,625 --> 00:31:59,417
Go home.

590
00:31:59,500 --> 00:32:00,793
Okay, Miss Camia.

591
00:32:06,883 --> 00:32:09,510
If Lily really were fine,
she would've called ages ago.

592
00:32:10,136 --> 00:32:12,305
What do you think
could've happened to her?

593
00:32:15,058 --> 00:32:17,644
[tense music playing]

594
00:32:23,024 --> 00:32:24,275
Here you go.

595
00:32:24,359 --> 00:32:25,401
Thank you.

596
00:32:26,069 --> 00:32:27,487
Let's get down to business.

597
00:32:30,031 --> 00:32:32,909
We want to file a complaint
to the election commission

598
00:32:33,242 --> 00:32:35,078
about Julio Ardiente's manipulation

599
00:32:35,161 --> 00:32:36,537
of the recent election results.

600
00:32:37,497 --> 00:32:39,332
And we need your support on this.

601
00:32:40,124 --> 00:32:41,834
[sighs]

602
00:32:41,918 --> 00:32:43,044
You see, Diego…

603
00:32:43,628 --> 00:32:45,630
That case is bailable.

604
00:32:45,922 --> 00:32:47,674
Even if you file a case against Julio,

605
00:32:48,049 --> 00:32:51,552
he'll just post bail, and your
efforts will be for nothing.

606
00:32:51,844 --> 00:32:53,513
We've already considered that.

607
00:32:53,930 --> 00:32:57,558
That's why we planned
something big against Julio.

608
00:32:57,850 --> 00:32:59,894
Once this gets out to the public,

609
00:32:59,978 --> 00:33:01,521
he'll be suspended,

610
00:33:01,604 --> 00:33:04,816
and you'll become governor of Ardiente.

611
00:33:05,817 --> 00:33:09,070
You're doing this even though
there's nothing in it for you?

612
00:33:10,029 --> 00:33:12,907
This isn't about my personal ambitions.

613
00:33:13,950 --> 00:33:16,577
It's about obtaining justice
for the people.

614
00:33:17,537 --> 00:33:20,164
So, Vice Governor,
I just want to make sure…

615
00:33:20,665 --> 00:33:22,667
that you're on the people's side.

616
00:33:23,543 --> 00:33:25,962
And that you're ready
to go against the Ardientes.

617
00:33:27,797 --> 00:33:31,050
[pensive music playing]

618
00:33:45,398 --> 00:33:48,192
[slow tense music playing]

619
00:33:57,994 --> 00:33:59,579
-Papa.
-Raul.

620
00:33:59,662 --> 00:34:01,080
Where are you taking Arnaldo?

621
00:34:01,164 --> 00:34:02,999
Oh, just for a little drive.

622
00:34:05,293 --> 00:34:07,378
Don't you think that'll be bad
for his health?

623
00:34:09,130 --> 00:34:10,673
Relax, Raul.

624
00:34:10,757 --> 00:34:12,592
I will take good care of him.

625
00:34:12,675 --> 00:34:17,305
And besides, it'll be better
if he went with me

626
00:34:17,388 --> 00:34:19,474
instead of staying here with you.

627
00:34:19,557 --> 00:34:20,475
[scoffs]

628
00:34:20,558 --> 00:34:21,601
Papa, Arnaldo's my son.

629
00:34:21,684 --> 00:34:24,103
I have the right to decide
whether or not he goes with you.

630
00:34:24,187 --> 00:34:25,646
Then, stop me.

631
00:34:26,147 --> 00:34:27,231
Stop them.

632
00:34:27,315 --> 00:34:29,192
[scoffs] Stop this guy.

633
00:34:29,275 --> 00:34:31,694
I've always had a problem controlling him.

634
00:34:32,195 --> 00:34:34,405
See? He always goes for his gun.

635
00:34:35,698 --> 00:34:37,116
Raul, Raul…

636
00:34:37,700 --> 00:34:40,161
You're the same old Raul as before.

637
00:34:40,870 --> 00:34:42,830
All bark, no bite.

638
00:34:44,082 --> 00:34:45,666
Balls, my boy. Balls.

639
00:34:46,000 --> 00:34:50,171
Try to grow a pair, and you
might just earn my respect

640
00:34:50,254 --> 00:34:52,757
as the father of your son.

641
00:34:53,216 --> 00:34:55,510
Now, if you'll excuse us…

642
00:34:55,593 --> 00:34:57,220
we'll be going now.

643
00:34:57,470 --> 00:34:58,513
Colonel.

644
00:35:00,598 --> 00:35:01,641
[Julio grunts]

645
00:35:03,893 --> 00:35:06,229
-[car engine starts]
-[car door closes]

646
00:35:18,491 --> 00:35:19,700
Ooh!

647
00:35:21,244 --> 00:35:22,286
Madrigal.

648
00:35:23,746 --> 00:35:26,582
What brings you here?

649
00:35:27,291 --> 00:35:28,376
Ma'am…

650
00:35:29,377 --> 00:35:31,254
I'm ready to return the favor now.

651
00:35:31,879 --> 00:35:33,214
You saved me, remember?

652
00:35:33,798 --> 00:35:35,216
What do you want in exchange?

653
00:35:39,220 --> 00:35:40,680
Hmm…

654
00:35:44,767 --> 00:35:46,435
Let me think.

655
00:35:47,478 --> 00:35:49,147
[sexy music playing]

656
00:35:51,315 --> 00:35:52,567
It depends.

657
00:35:54,569 --> 00:35:55,903
What exactly…

658
00:35:59,490 --> 00:36:01,117
…can you do?

659
00:36:03,244 --> 00:36:05,079
Can you make me…

660
00:36:05,413 --> 00:36:06,622
happy?

661
00:36:11,711 --> 00:36:13,296
Give me weapons, ma'am.

662
00:36:13,921 --> 00:36:15,006
And some men.

663
00:36:16,215 --> 00:36:18,467
I'll help you get back at the Ardientes.

664
00:36:21,804 --> 00:36:23,890
I like the idea.

665
00:36:26,058 --> 00:36:28,019
But what about Jaguar?

666
00:36:28,728 --> 00:36:30,479
He almost killed you.

667
00:36:32,190 --> 00:36:33,983
Aren't you interested…

668
00:36:35,443 --> 00:36:38,029
in making him pay for what he did to you?

669
00:36:40,156 --> 00:36:42,033
Aren't you curious

670
00:36:42,658 --> 00:36:46,454
as to who he really is?

671
00:36:47,288 --> 00:36:49,248
As to who the man is

672
00:36:49,749 --> 00:36:51,751
behind that mask?

673
00:36:52,960 --> 00:36:54,670
By the way you talk, ma'am,

674
00:36:55,880 --> 00:36:57,715
you sound like you know him.

675
00:36:59,342 --> 00:37:00,593
[chuckles]

676
00:37:00,676 --> 00:37:02,845
Of course I know who he is.

677
00:37:04,305 --> 00:37:07,516
I'm the reason why he's
roaming free right now.

678
00:37:08,351 --> 00:37:10,228
After all the help I gave him,

679
00:37:10,895 --> 00:37:12,897
he just cast me aside.

680
00:37:14,273 --> 00:37:15,274
In that case,

681
00:37:16,150 --> 00:37:18,319
why don't you tell me who he is?

682
00:37:21,322 --> 00:37:22,657
I can help you.

683
00:37:24,200 --> 00:37:26,327
[slow tense music playing]

684
00:37:36,712 --> 00:37:38,089
Emilia!

685
00:37:38,172 --> 00:37:39,757
-Mr. Raul.
-Emilia!

686
00:37:39,840 --> 00:37:40,758
Sir--

687
00:37:40,841 --> 00:37:43,511
Why'd Emilia let Papa take Arnaldo, huh?!

688
00:37:43,594 --> 00:37:45,346
And you didn't even bother to call me?

689
00:37:45,429 --> 00:37:46,806
Where's Emilia?! Go call her!

690
00:37:46,889 --> 00:37:48,557
She's not here, sir.

691
00:37:48,641 --> 00:37:49,892
She left early.

692
00:37:51,310 --> 00:37:52,353
Where did she go?

693
00:37:52,436 --> 00:37:54,021
I don't know, sir.

694
00:37:54,105 --> 00:37:55,439
Please excuse me.

695
00:37:56,816 --> 00:37:59,110
[tense music playing]

696
00:38:06,200 --> 00:38:08,911
Uh-uh-uh…

697
00:38:09,662 --> 00:38:11,789
Not that fast, Madrigal.

698
00:38:13,249 --> 00:38:14,667
Hmm…

699
00:38:14,750 --> 00:38:16,919
It's not going to be that easy.

700
00:38:17,628 --> 00:38:19,422
You have to work hard for it.

701
00:38:20,673 --> 00:38:23,134
You have to earn my trust.

702
00:38:23,217 --> 00:38:24,719
And, when you get it,

703
00:38:26,012 --> 00:38:29,640
I might just tell you everything I know.

704
00:38:30,725 --> 00:38:32,560
You know, to be honest,

705
00:38:32,643 --> 00:38:34,895
Jaguar doesn't really mean
anything to me right now.

706
00:38:36,439 --> 00:38:38,399
Julio's the one we should focus on.

707
00:38:39,066 --> 00:38:41,694
He's the one in charge,
so we must get to him first.

708
00:38:42,945 --> 00:38:45,364
Why not kill two birds with one stone?

709
00:38:45,448 --> 00:38:47,825
Julio and Jaguar…

710
00:38:49,243 --> 00:38:51,329
I can't wait for their downfall.

711
00:38:54,165 --> 00:38:56,083
And, if you do that,

712
00:38:57,585 --> 00:38:59,920
I might just give you a reward.

713
00:39:01,630 --> 00:39:03,716
Do you want to know what it is?

714
00:39:05,134 --> 00:39:07,011
Well, do you?

715
00:39:09,263 --> 00:39:10,681
Do you want to have…

716
00:39:12,892 --> 00:39:14,101
a taste?

717
00:39:14,727 --> 00:39:16,937
[slow tense music playing]

718
00:39:30,034 --> 00:39:31,327
With all due respect, ma'am…

719
00:39:33,662 --> 00:39:35,414
I couldn't care about the money.

720
00:39:36,874 --> 00:39:38,084
All that matters to me

721
00:39:38,167 --> 00:39:41,128
is killing Julio Ardiente and Jaguar…

722
00:39:41,212 --> 00:39:43,172
so I can protect the ones I love.

723
00:39:43,506 --> 00:39:44,882
That's all there is to it.

724
00:39:47,927 --> 00:39:49,470
I hope we can work together.

725
00:39:55,601 --> 00:39:56,852
I'll be going now.

726
00:39:57,937 --> 00:40:00,606
[suspenseful music playing]

727
00:40:13,786 --> 00:40:14,870
[door closes]

728
00:40:19,333 --> 00:40:20,668
[sighs]

729
00:40:26,006 --> 00:40:27,508
That damned woman!

730
00:40:28,175 --> 00:40:29,927
She almost smashed my face in!

731
00:40:31,220 --> 00:40:32,096
Smashed it in?

732
00:40:32,179 --> 00:40:33,431
Then you would've looked better.

733
00:40:33,514 --> 00:40:35,266
-[guffaws]
-Hey!

734
00:40:36,308 --> 00:40:38,144
Want to get back at her?

735
00:40:38,727 --> 00:40:39,770
How?

736
00:40:41,397 --> 00:40:42,273
[scoffs]

737
00:40:47,069 --> 00:40:47,987
Come.

738
00:40:49,697 --> 00:40:51,449
[foreboding music playing]

739
00:40:52,825 --> 00:40:54,452
All right, grab her!

740
00:40:55,035 --> 00:40:56,078
[laughing]

741
00:40:56,162 --> 00:40:56,912
[goon] Don't fight back.

742
00:40:56,996 --> 00:40:58,247
Time to get our reward.

743
00:40:59,039 --> 00:41:02,501
You better make sure
I don't get out of here alive.

744
00:41:03,794 --> 00:41:05,796
Or else, I'm going to make you pay.

745
00:41:06,130 --> 00:41:07,840
-[mocking laughter]
-Hurry up! Go!

746
00:41:08,340 --> 00:41:09,425
Hold her tight.

747
00:41:10,050 --> 00:41:11,635
Dude, hurry up!

748
00:41:12,344 --> 00:41:14,346
[suspenseful music playing]

749
00:41:16,849 --> 00:41:18,142
[gunshot]

750
00:41:20,144 --> 00:41:21,520
[chuckles]

751
00:41:22,897 --> 00:41:25,941
Party's over, boys!

752
00:41:32,948 --> 00:41:34,366
Diego, son…

753
00:41:34,450 --> 00:41:39,205
You have to take the position
when Julio gets ousted.

754
00:41:39,288 --> 00:41:44,376
We don't know
Vice Governor Mateo Ruiz well.

755
00:41:44,460 --> 00:41:46,253
Can we really trust him?

756
00:41:46,629 --> 00:41:48,756
Nanny, his track record is clean.

757
00:41:48,839 --> 00:41:52,593
And he's a better choice
because he's not an Ardiente.

758
00:41:52,676 --> 00:41:56,514
But what about your dream
to be the governor?

759
00:41:58,015 --> 00:42:00,351
Uncle, I can sacrifice my dream…

760
00:42:01,477 --> 00:42:03,354
if it's for the people's freedom.

761
00:42:06,023 --> 00:42:08,192
Hey, Batch, watch this.

762
00:42:09,902 --> 00:42:12,154
[reporter] <i>A truck carrying stolen rice</i>

763
00:42:12,238 --> 00:42:13,822
<i>worth two million pesos</i>

764
00:42:13,906 --> 00:42:16,992
<i>was seized by the police during a storm,</i>

765
00:42:17,076 --> 00:42:19,119
<i>under the orders of Vice</i>
<i>Governor Mateo Ruiz.</i>

766
00:42:19,203 --> 00:42:20,955
<i>Here's his statement.</i>

767
00:42:21,038 --> 00:42:25,334
<i>We will subdue all thefts</i>
<i>here in Ardiente.</i>

768
00:42:25,417 --> 00:42:28,295
<i>This is one of the reasons</i>
<i>why our province isn't truly prospering.</i>

769
00:42:28,379 --> 00:42:31,840
<i>Big fish or two-bit hustlers,</i>
<i>if you're a criminal…</i>

770
00:42:32,758 --> 00:42:35,469
<i>don't bother trying to swim here,</i>

771
00:42:35,553 --> 00:42:37,555
<i>because I promise you…</i>

772
00:42:37,888 --> 00:42:39,265
<i>I will catch you.</i>

773
00:42:39,348 --> 00:42:40,140
[chuckles]

774
00:42:40,224 --> 00:42:41,976
The guy's pretty tough, then.

775
00:42:42,059 --> 00:42:44,395
He's like a fearless action star.

776
00:42:44,478 --> 00:42:46,146
Just like you. [chuckles]

777
00:42:46,230 --> 00:42:47,690
He's the man we need

778
00:42:47,773 --> 00:42:50,025
to take down the Ardientes.

779
00:42:51,068 --> 00:42:52,278
-It looks like it.
-Yeah.

780
00:42:55,197 --> 00:42:57,116
Useless morons!

781
00:42:57,199 --> 00:43:00,160
And you, cowering at the back!

782
00:43:00,244 --> 00:43:02,246
Useless! Idiots!

783
00:43:02,329 --> 00:43:04,123
How did Ivy get away from you?

784
00:43:05,541 --> 00:43:07,126
Governor, somebody helped her.

785
00:43:07,626 --> 00:43:09,211
[Julio] Somebody helped her? Who?

786
00:43:09,295 --> 00:43:11,505
Was it Madrigal again?! Or maybe Diego?!

787
00:43:12,506 --> 00:43:13,507
It was Mrs. Emilia.

788
00:43:13,591 --> 00:43:14,925
What?

789
00:43:15,217 --> 00:43:16,719
[tense music playing]

790
00:43:27,479 --> 00:43:28,606
Hey, Emilia.

791
00:43:28,689 --> 00:43:30,065
Where are you taking me?

792
00:43:30,983 --> 00:43:33,277
Hey, Ivy. Sit back and shut up.

793
00:43:33,694 --> 00:43:34,987
Don't be so impatient.

794
00:43:35,070 --> 00:43:37,281
And don't you just love surprises?

795
00:43:37,364 --> 00:43:38,449
Come on.

796
00:43:38,532 --> 00:43:39,908
Party pooper.

797
00:43:40,618 --> 00:43:42,953
Impatient? You want
to see me get impatient?

798
00:43:43,037 --> 00:43:44,246
You want to see a surprise?

799
00:43:45,706 --> 00:43:47,416
Let me go…

800
00:43:48,250 --> 00:43:50,711
so I can surprise you with
what I'm going to do to you.

801
00:43:51,587 --> 00:43:52,880
Uh-uh!

802
00:43:52,963 --> 00:43:54,465
No, thank you, Ivy.

803
00:43:54,548 --> 00:43:56,091
But this is your day.

804
00:43:56,175 --> 00:43:57,760
This is your big, big day!

805
00:43:57,843 --> 00:43:59,386
This is just for you.

806
00:43:59,470 --> 00:44:01,555
I'm not going to steal your thunder.

807
00:44:01,639 --> 00:44:03,641
You'll be surprised.

808
00:44:03,724 --> 00:44:05,309
Stay put, okay?

809
00:44:05,392 --> 00:44:06,143
Relax!

810
00:44:06,226 --> 00:44:07,811
We're almost there.

811
00:44:07,895 --> 00:44:09,313
[mocking laugh]

812
00:44:12,775 --> 00:44:19,448
[church bells ringing]

813
00:44:23,661 --> 00:44:27,081
[motorcycle engines revving]

814
00:44:29,750 --> 00:44:30,876
[phone ringing]

815
00:44:30,959 --> 00:44:33,462
Oops, I have a phone call.

816
00:44:33,545 --> 00:44:35,923
-[phone ringing]
-Oh! It's Papa.

817
00:44:36,215 --> 00:44:37,424
Hello, Papa.

818
00:44:37,925 --> 00:44:40,844
Emilia, Emilia…

819
00:44:40,928 --> 00:44:44,932
<i>…my she-devil of a daughter, Emilia.</i>

820
00:44:45,391 --> 00:44:47,726
According to my men,

821
00:44:47,810 --> 00:44:50,437
you did something stupid again.

822
00:44:50,979 --> 00:44:54,191
Papa, it was just a little prank.

823
00:44:54,274 --> 00:44:57,486
And Ivy is with me right now.

824
00:44:57,569 --> 00:44:58,320
[chuckles]

825
00:44:58,404 --> 00:44:59,780
Where are you taking her?

826
00:44:59,863 --> 00:45:00,948
Hmm…

827
00:45:01,031 --> 00:45:02,616
I don't want to tell you, Papa.

828
00:45:02,699 --> 00:45:05,953
Because I know you're going
to take Ivy from me again

829
00:45:06,036 --> 00:45:08,247
and you'll do what you want with her.

830
00:45:08,330 --> 00:45:09,915
So, I'm not going to tell you.

831
00:45:10,332 --> 00:45:11,208
<i>Emilia…</i>

832
00:45:11,291 --> 00:45:14,086
…you don't have to keep her from me.

833
00:45:15,504 --> 00:45:17,589
<i>She's my enemy too.</i>

834
00:45:18,340 --> 00:45:21,552
We both want her dead.

835
00:45:21,635 --> 00:45:22,803
<i>Look…</i>

836
00:45:22,886 --> 00:45:24,972
<i>If you want her…</i>

837
00:45:25,472 --> 00:45:28,434
Go ahead. You can have her.

838
00:45:28,517 --> 00:45:30,185
<i>I don't mind.</i>

839
00:45:30,269 --> 00:45:31,770
<i>It's just that…</i>

840
00:45:33,188 --> 00:45:35,983
I want Arnaldo to witness…

841
00:45:37,151 --> 00:45:39,903
that woman's death.

842
00:45:39,987 --> 00:45:41,113
Do you understand me?

843
00:45:41,697 --> 00:45:43,657
Ooh!

844
00:45:43,740 --> 00:45:45,534
Do you swear on that, Papa?

845
00:45:45,617 --> 00:45:47,286
You're just gonna be an audience?

846
00:45:47,369 --> 00:45:49,538
You're not gonna do anything else?

847
00:45:49,621 --> 00:45:53,959
I swear on the grave of my parents.

848
00:45:54,460 --> 00:45:56,462
I won't interfere.

849
00:45:56,962 --> 00:45:58,797
[laughs excitedly]

850
00:45:58,881 --> 00:46:00,340
Okay, Papa!

851
00:46:00,424 --> 00:46:01,925
It's a done deal!

852
00:46:02,009 --> 00:46:04,344
I shall see you, then.

853
00:46:04,428 --> 00:46:06,972
[Emilia laughs excitedly]

854
00:46:07,055 --> 00:46:09,141
[suspenseful music playing]

855
00:46:12,728 --> 00:46:13,854
Woohoo!

856
00:46:13,937 --> 00:46:15,314
This is it!

857
00:46:16,106 --> 00:46:17,483
Yeah, yeah, yeah!

858
00:46:17,566 --> 00:46:18,692
We're near.

859
00:46:19,318 --> 00:46:20,861
Don't celebrate just yet, Emilia,

860
00:46:20,944 --> 00:46:22,988
because when I get
out of here, I'll kill you

861
00:46:23,071 --> 00:46:24,615
and leave your body to rot!

862
00:46:24,698 --> 00:46:25,824
Ha!

863
00:46:25,908 --> 00:46:27,701
[mockingly] I'm so scared.

864
00:46:27,784 --> 00:46:29,661
Yes, you should be scared!

865
00:46:32,831 --> 00:46:34,750
[Emilia guffaws]

866
00:46:34,833 --> 00:46:36,919
We're here!

867
00:46:37,544 --> 00:46:39,004
This is it!

868
00:46:40,339 --> 00:46:42,508
How did your meeting with the attorney go?

869
00:46:42,591 --> 00:46:44,218
I was able to talk to the vice governor.

870
00:46:44,301 --> 00:46:47,304
He said he'll consider
forming an alliance with us.

871
00:46:48,639 --> 00:46:50,182
Any news about Ivy?

872
00:46:50,766 --> 00:46:51,767
That's the problem, Diego.

873
00:46:51,850 --> 00:46:53,519
We haven't found her yet.

874
00:46:54,603 --> 00:46:55,604
What?

875
00:46:59,274 --> 00:47:03,111
[unsettling music playing]

876
00:47:06,865 --> 00:47:09,451
[Ivy grunting]

877
00:47:09,993 --> 00:47:12,120
Stand up, Ivy! Get up!

878
00:47:13,789 --> 00:47:14,831
[groans]

879
00:47:15,332 --> 00:47:16,250
Move!

880
00:47:17,543 --> 00:47:19,002
[Ivy panting]

881
00:47:19,670 --> 00:47:21,630
Walk. Stop making a fuss!

882
00:47:21,713 --> 00:47:23,549
Stop fighting!

883
00:47:24,174 --> 00:47:25,133
Come here.

884
00:47:26,051 --> 00:47:27,010
Well, now…

885
00:47:27,094 --> 00:47:28,637
Let's see how tough you are.

886
00:47:28,720 --> 00:47:30,472
What will you do to me?! Huh?!

887
00:47:30,556 --> 00:47:32,015
You'll find out soon enough.

888
00:47:32,558 --> 00:47:36,979
You'll see where I'm taking you, witch!

889
00:47:37,062 --> 00:47:38,105
Move it!

890
00:47:40,357 --> 00:47:42,109
[laughing]

891
00:47:42,734 --> 00:47:48,115
[Emilia laughs boisterously]

892
00:47:49,116 --> 00:47:50,867
-[Emilia sighs]
-Emilia, you witch!

893
00:47:50,951 --> 00:47:52,077
Where are we?!

894
00:47:52,869 --> 00:47:54,246
Oh, pipe down.

895
00:47:54,788 --> 00:47:55,664
Shh!

896
00:47:56,498 --> 00:47:57,666
Where are we?

897
00:47:57,749 --> 00:47:59,626
Ivy, stop asking questions.

898
00:47:59,710 --> 00:48:04,047
You'll know later after your last breath.

899
00:48:04,131 --> 00:48:06,508
[giggles]

900
00:48:07,175 --> 00:48:08,635
You witch!

901
00:48:08,719 --> 00:48:15,851
-[Emilia laughs maniacally]
-[suspenseful music playing]

902
00:48:23,358 --> 00:48:27,237
[Emilia] <i>It's going to be</i>
<i>Ivy's funeral, Papa.</i>

903
00:48:27,321 --> 00:48:29,448
<i>Ivy is dying today?!</i>

904
00:48:30,574 --> 00:48:32,784
[Ivy] <i>What are you doing to me?!</i>
<i>Let go of me!</i>

905
00:48:32,868 --> 00:48:35,621
[mockingly] <i>No, sir, no.</i>
<i>Please, don't leave me, Ivy.</i>

906
00:48:35,704 --> 00:48:36,455
<i>Please!</i>

907
00:48:36,538 --> 00:48:39,416
[fake cries, laughs maniacally]

908
00:48:39,499 --> 00:48:41,084
[Raul] <i>Ivy Aguas is in danger.</i>

909
00:48:41,168 --> 00:48:42,586
<i>The Ardientes buried her alive.</i>

910
00:48:42,669 --> 00:48:43,754
<i>What?</i>

911
00:48:43,837 --> 00:48:44,963
-[Camia screaming]
-[glass breaking]

912
00:48:45,047 --> 00:48:47,966
<i>They buried her alive</i>
<i>just like they did to me!</i>

913
00:48:48,050 --> 00:48:50,260
[Damian] <i>Now that I'm here, I'll help you.</i>

914
00:48:50,344 --> 00:48:52,387
<i>I'll find your daughter.</i>

915
00:48:52,471 --> 00:48:56,266
[Ivy wheezing, crying]

916
00:48:56,350 --> 00:48:58,477
[theme music playing]
